<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
	The hold, the second half of an inspection.

	TienInspectWeapon.xml is the wind-up: the character brings the weapon up and turns it
	over once, and when that finishes the window opens and this node takes over for as long
	as the player is reading. Two nodes rather than one because the two halves are doing
	different things - one is an action with a duration, the other is a pose being held -
	and because a single clip stretched across both reads as a loop nobody chose.

	Bob_IdleLookAtPhoto is a character holding something up in front of them and studying
	it, which is the gesture this mod is after and is not something any of the looting clips
	quite manage - those are rummaging motions, hands passing over things rather than
	settling on one.

	It being a genuine Idle clip matters as much as the pose does. The hold can run for the
	whole sandbox ceiling, so it has to survive looping, and an idle is authored to do
	exactly that where an action clip is authored to finish. That is also why m_SpeedScale
	is 1.0 here: the clip is already paced as something a character does at rest, so there
	is nothing to slow down.

	m_Looped is true here and false everywhere in vanilla's actions folder, because every
	vanilla action is short enough to finish. This one is not, and the game's own idle, walk
	and run nodes are the precedent for a node that has to keep going.

	No m_SubStateBoneWeights, for the same reason TienInspectWeapon.xml has none - see the
	comment there.
-->
<animNode>
	<m_Name>TienInspectWeaponHold</m_Name>
	<m_AnimName>Bob_IdleLookAtPhoto</m_AnimName>
	<m_Looped>true</m_Looped>
	<m_BlendTime>0.30</m_BlendTime>
	<m_SpeedScale>1.0</m_SpeedScale>
	<m_SyncTrackingEnabled>false</m_SyncTrackingEnabled>
	<m_Conditions x_name="3e59b7c4-8a12-4f6d-b0e7-2c9d41f8a6b3">
		<m_Name>PerformingAction</m_Name>
		<m_Type>STRING</m_Type>
		<m_Value>TienInspectWeaponHold</m_Value>
	</m_Conditions>
</animNode>
